<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grand Council (Qing)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1729</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Grand Council</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grand Council was a small advisory body established by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yongzheng-emperor">Yongzheng Emperor</a> around c. 1729. It handled sensitive military and political matters and concentrated decision-making in the emperor's hands, becoming the most important organ of government in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> link reflects the separate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-council-of-fascism">Grand Council of Fascism</a>.</p></div>
